<header><h1>Objective Cards: Proof</h1></header>
<article>
<p>The source text behind each note on <a href="/R_objective_cards">Objective Cards</a>. <b>Explicit</b> sources state the note directly. <b>Implicit</b> sources support it without stating it.</p>

<h2>Notes</h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A status phase objective must have its condition met during the status phase.<sup>1,2,3</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can I mark an objective as soon as I meet it and score it later &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;You must qualify at the moment you score. Status-phase objectives check the condition then.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 61.5a: &ldquo;When a player scores an objective during the status phase, they must fulfill the requirement on the card during the &ldquo;Score Objectives&rdquo; step of the status phase to score that objective.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>3</sup> Learn to Play: &ldquo;requirement on the card during the &lsquo;Score Objectives&rsquo; step of the status phase to score that objective.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Any number of players may score a given public objective during the status phase.<sup>2,3</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Do revealed public objectives stay in play, and can several players score the same one?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Any number of players can score each, but each player scores a given objective only once.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>3</sup> Learn to Play: &ldquo;Any number of players can score each of these objectives.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player may score an action phase secret objective when they are not the active player.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How and when are action-phase secret objectives scored?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Secret objectives marked Action Phase are scored the moment you meet them, even on another player&rsquo;s turn and even after you have passed.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 61.5b: &ldquo;When a player scores an objective during the action phase, they can do so at any time during that phase.&rdquo; any time in the phase, not limited to own turn.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If two players could each score an action phase objective during the same combat, the player whose condition is met first scores first; for example, a flagship or war sun is destroyed during a combat round, before the combat ends and has a winner. If both conditions are met at the same moment, the active player scores first.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;If two players could each score an action-phase objective in the same combat, who scores first?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Whichever condition is met first. Destroying a flagship or war sun happens during a combat round, before the combat ends and has a winner.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <b>Bombardment</b> and <b>Space Cannon</b> steps happen outside of combat.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Which kills trigger Nekro&rsquo;s Technological Singularity?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Kills from Space Cannon, Bombardment &hellip; happen outside combat.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR Movement, Step 2: &ldquo;Space Cannon Offense: After the Move Ships step, players can use the Space Cannon abilities of their units in the active system.&rdquo; Space combat is a later step of the tactical action.</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR Invasion: &ldquo;Step 1 &ndash; Bombardment&rdquo; and &ldquo;Step 3 &ndash; Space Cannon Defense&rdquo; come before &ldquo;Step 4 &ndash; Ground Combat.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>The <b>Anti&ndash;Fighter Barrage</b> step, however, is a step during combat.<sup>1,2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> Same entry: &ldquo;Anti-Fighter Barrage is part of combat and counts.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR Space Combat: &ldquo;Step 1 &ndash; Anti-Fighter Barrage: If this is the first round of a space combat, the players may simultaneously use the Anti-Fighter Barrage ability of any of their units in the active system.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (livestrongbelwas, Feb 08, 2018): &ldquo;Anti-Fighter Barrage, which is its own distinct timing (essentially the first step of combat)&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>A player with three scored secret objectives may draw a fourth. However, they must immediately shuffle it into the secret objective deck.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, on the scored-secret limit: &ldquo;you could draw an additional secret but would then need to return it and shuffle the secret objective deck.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 45.4: &ldquo;If a player has more than three secret objective cards after drawing a secret objective, they must choose one of their unscored secret objectives and return it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The number of secret objective cards in a player&rsquo;s hand is public information.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player may choose to reveal any or all of their unscored secret objectives to other players.<sup>1,2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Can you intentionally reveal hidden information to another player, such as &hellip; your secret objective? A: Yes. This information is kept hidden by default, but it is permissible to reveal it.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can I show my action cards or secret objectives to other players?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; you may reveal your own hidden cards to anyone at any time, and they still count as hidden afterwards.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (x3n d0g, 1/25/2019): &ldquo;If you feel you have a reason to show someone a card, perhaps as part ot a negotiation or to convince them to do something for you, that is your prerogative and I would prefer not to restrict that.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
</article>
